e fact that $ \\triangle DEF $ is an isosceles triangle with $ DE = EF = DF $. Since $ D, E, $ and $ F $ are midpoints, we have:\n\n$$\nDE = EF = DF = \\frac{1}{2} a = \\frac{a}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\widehat{EF} = 2 \\arcsin \\left( \\frac{\\frac{a}{2}}{2R} \\right) = 2 \\arcsin \\left( \\frac{a}{4R} \\right)\n$$\n\nFinally, we can find the desired sum:\n\n$$\n\\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} = 3 \\widehat{EF} = 3 \\cdot 2 \\arcsin \\left( \\frac{a}{4R} \\right) = 6 \\arcsin \\left( \\frac{a}{4R} \\right)\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $ \\frac{a}{4R} $, we need to use the fact that $ a = 2R \\sin 36^\\circ $ and $ b = 2R \\sin 60^\\circ $. Therefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{4R} = \\frac{2R \\sin 36^\\circ}{4R} = \\frac{1}{2} \\sin 36^\\circ\n$$\n\nFinally, we can find the desired sum:\n\n$$\n\\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} = 6 \\arcsin \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\sin 36^\\circ \\right)\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator, we find:\n\n$$\n\\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} \\approx 6 \\arcsin \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\sin 36^\\circ \\right) \\approx 6 \\cdot 18.43^\\circ \\approx 110.58^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{110.58^\\circ}\n$$",
